WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:04.920
Westworld Season 3 Episode 7 starts with..

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:05.920
Musashi..

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:12.940
-Sato.. -lores – his mind is a copy of Dolores,
his body is Musashi’s from Shogunworld,

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:18.350
and he’s pretending to be a Yakuza boss
called Sato . Musatolores sends a package

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:23.640
to a mysterious “friend” in a mysterious
“location” . We know there was communication

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:28.630
between “Jakarta, Berlin, San Francisco,
and Los Angeles” – Dolores and Martin-lores

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:34.809
were in LA, Charlotte-lores was in San Fran,
Musashi-lores is now in Jakarta, so maybe

00:00:34.809 --> 00:00:38.320
this “friend” is a Dolores copy in Berlin.

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:42.620
Maybe Musashi is working with him to create
more hosts with that white goo.

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:47.160
But whose body does this Berlin host have?

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:53.250
Musashi refers to him as male, so maybe he’s
Teddy, or maybe Lawrence – it looks like

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:58.989
his actor may return this season . So the
fifth and final Dolores copy could be..

00:00:58.989 --> 00:01:01.289
Lawrence-lores.

00:01:01.289 --> 00:01:06.549
Charlotte-lores betrays Musashi by leaking
his location to Hanaryo and Clementine, who

00:01:06.549 --> 00:01:11.939
were printed by Serac last episode to help
Maeve kill the Doloreses.

00:01:11.939 --> 00:01:16.369
Charlotte is angry at Dolores for risking
her life , and says she has her own “plan”

00:01:16.369 --> 00:01:21.900
now . But last episode, Charlotte and her
family were blown up by Serac – so why would

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:25.270
Charlotte help Serac kill Doloreses?

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:28.609
Maybe Charlotte thinks that Dolores killed
her family.

00:01:28.609 --> 00:01:33.899
Maybe Serac turned Charlotte against Dolores,
just like he turned Maeve against Dolores.

00:01:33.899 --> 00:01:36.889
Or maybe this isn’t even Charlotte.

00:01:36.889 --> 00:01:38.649
Last episode, Charlotte was burned.

00:01:38.649 --> 00:01:43.859
Now, she looks partly healed, but the lighting
is dark and weird.

00:01:43.859 --> 00:01:49.979
Maybe this is just a hologram, or Charlotte
is somehow controlled by Serac.

00:01:49.979 --> 00:01:52.159
Musashi-lores is killed by Hanaryo.

00:01:52.159 --> 00:01:53.979
This is personal for her.

00:01:53.979 --> 00:01:57.770
Because Hanaryo was allies with the real Musashi
in Shogunworld.

00:01:57.770 --> 00:02:04.090
So it’s horrible for her to see her friends’
face being worn by Dolores – he “desecrated”

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:08.899
the real Musashi’s “image” . Hanaryo
takes Musashi-lores’ head.

00:02:08.899 --> 00:02:11.890
And we know Charlotte-lores has Martin-lores’
brain.

00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:16.459
So maybe there’ll be a reunion of all the
Doloreses .

00:02:16.459 --> 00:02:19.849
We see Clementine acting normally, which is
weird.

00:02:19.849 --> 00:02:26.310
Cause in Season 1, Clementine was lobotomised,
her brain was wiped, and she was later programmed

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:28.430
to be a mindless death zombie.

00:02:28.430 --> 00:02:34.370
And in Season 2, the host backups in the Cradle
were destroyed . So how was Clementine restored

00:02:34.370 --> 00:02:35.730
to her normal self?

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:41.430
Do she and Hanaryo really have free will here,
or are they pawns being used by Maeve and

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:42.560
Serac?

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:48.579
This episode is called Passed Pawn, and it’s
all about control.

00:02:48.579 --> 00:02:50.040
Dolores and Caleb go to Mexico.

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:54.120
Cause it turns out that that blood “tracker”
in William last episode?

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:58.659
– its purpose wasn’t to track William
– he’s just in San Francisco – its purpose

00:02:58.659 --> 00:03:02.750
was to hack into computers there to find [the
location of] this other facility in Mexico

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:05.230
, where Dolores and Caleb go [to recover Caleb’s
memories and find Solomon] .

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:10.340
Caleb casually reveals that he knows that
Dolores is a host who killed a bunch of people

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:14.799
in Westworld . He mighta worked it out when
he saw Dolores get shot, and he mighta seen

00:03:14.799 --> 00:03:16.769
the news about the Westworld massacre.

00:03:16.769 --> 00:03:22.730
But he seems really relaxed about the fact
that his new pal is a murderous robot.

00:03:22.730 --> 00:03:27.019
He asks her what her revolution is about , and
Dolores says that she just wants a place for

00:03:27.019 --> 00:03:32.489
the hosts to be “free” . She says Westworld
was based on this wild west landscape – that

00:03:32.489 --> 00:03:38.409
while “The West was… cruel, unjust, and
chaotic”, it also had hope and freedom . Dolores

00:03:38.409 --> 00:03:43.120
wants land and opportunity for her people
, just as American settlers looked for land

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:44.599
and opportunity.

00:03:44.599 --> 00:03:49.760
But just like the settlers, she brings violence
and death as well as hope.

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:55.049
Caleb questions how many people will die for
her revolution .

00:03:55.049 --> 00:03:59.950
Dolores tells Caleb to be a leader – she
wants him to carry out her plan of revolution

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:06.310
. But Bernard says this plan will actually
“destroy humanity” . So Dolores is manipulating

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:10.609
Caleb – using him to lead humanity into
slaughter.

00:04:10.609 --> 00:04:13.620
Which connects to a similar scene in Season
1.

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:19.299
Dolores tells Teddy that farmers control herds
of cows with a “Judas steer” – you control

00:04:19.299 --> 00:04:26.099
the Judas steer to lead the herd to the slaughterhouse
. So Caleb is that Judas steer, leading humanity

00:04:26.099 --> 00:04:27.590
to its doom.

00:04:27.590 --> 00:04:32.330
While Bernard is trying to protect the humans
– like he tried to help a cow in Episode

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:35.979
1 .
Dolores uses a fancy gun with a target-spotting

00:04:35.979 --> 00:04:39.590
drone to kill some guards and get inside the
facility.

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:44.199
This is the same facility that we saw in a
flashback – it’s where Serac takes unpredictable

00:04:44.199 --> 00:04:49.690
people called outliers, and edits them to
make them more controllable . Caleb starts

00:04:49.690 --> 00:04:54.060
to remember that he too was edited here.

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:56.440
Dolores came here to find Solomon.

00:04:56.440 --> 00:05:02.690
Solomon is an earlier version of Rehoboam,
the AI supercomputer that controls the world.

00:05:02.690 --> 00:05:08.180
It was created by Jean Mi and Serac, but Jean
Mi became “mad” , “chaotic” , and

00:05:08.180 --> 00:05:13.330
“schizophrenic” – and his computer Solomon
became unstable like him . So Solomon was

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:16.410
replaced with the more orderly Rehoboam.

00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:21.980
Solomon recognises Caleb, because Solomon
knows potential futures from his data projections.

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:28.121
But Solomon’s not sure what’s real – if
this is “now”, if this is “here” . Back

00:05:28.121 --> 00:05:33.360
in Season 1, Dolores asked herself the same
questions, when she was becoming conscious

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:39.319
. So Solomon’s ‘instability’ might actually
be his path to consciousness.

00:05:39.319 --> 00:05:45.229
Co-showrunner Jonathan Nolan has talked about
leaving a mind in a box until it goes insane,

00:05:45.229 --> 00:05:50.430
and how that insanity might have truth to
it – which is basically what’s happening

00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:51.430
to Solomon.

00:05:51.430 --> 00:05:55.830
It seems that Solomon doesn’t directly know
what’s happening in the world anymore, it

00:05:55.830 --> 00:06:01.050
can only guess what’s happening based on
old predictions . It’s kinda like Plato’s

00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:06.430
allegory of the cave, where someone can’t
see reality directly, they only see shadows

00:06:06.430 --> 00:06:12.520
of a simulated reality . If one escapes the
cave, they can see real world directly – like

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:15.199
how Dolores and Maeve have escaped Westworld.

00:06:15.199 --> 00:06:21.449
The season premiere alluded to Plato’s cave,
with this crazy guy shouting about “Shadow

00:06:21.449 --> 00:06:27.009
people” , and seeing “the light” .
Dolores says that she and Solomon are alike

00:06:27.009 --> 00:06:32.469
– they’ve both considered obsolete technology
. And they’ve both been trapped and controlled

00:06:32.469 --> 00:06:37.690
. Dolores once had an explosive in her spine
that would go off if she tried to escape – which

00:06:37.690 --> 00:06:40.360
is why she touches the back of her neck here.

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:44.879
And Solomon is trapped by the threat of an
EMP that’s set to disable him if he tries

00:06:44.879 --> 00:06:50.830
to leave . But Solomon rejects Dolores and
says they’re nothing alike . The same thing

00:06:50.830 --> 00:06:56.099
happens later when Dolores tries to make peace
with Maeve, and Maeve says they’re “nothing

00:06:56.099 --> 00:07:00.389
alike” . Turns out, it’s hard to make
friends when you’re an extremist robot in

00:07:00.389 --> 00:07:02.240
a revolutionary war.

00:07:02.240 --> 00:07:07.310
All Dolores has are enemies, and allies who
she uses for her plans.

00:07:07.310 --> 00:07:10.710
We learn more about Serac’s reconditioning
program.

00:07:10.710 --> 00:07:16.060
He takes “outliers” who don’t fit into
his system, and gives them AR therapy to “reprogram”

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:21.000
them , make them controllable and predictable
. With most of these patients, the treatment

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:26.630
doesn’t work , so Serac has them frozen
in this facility – thousands of people kept

00:07:26.630 --> 00:07:32.500
in stasis, just like cold storage in Westworld,
where malfunctioning hosts go . Humans are

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:34.919
controlled like hosts.

00:07:34.919 --> 00:07:40.449
And the centrepiece of this place is the frozen
sarcophagus of Jean Mi, Serac’s beloved

00:07:40.449 --> 00:07:43.300
brother who he failed to reprogram and “fix”.

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:48.090
Solomon speaks with Jean Mi’s voice, and
has Jean Mi’s personality.

00:07:48.090 --> 00:07:53.610
So Solomon is like a machine version of Jean
Mi, in same way that Bernard is a machine

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:55.199
version of Arnold.

00:07:55.199 --> 00:08:01.360
Ford’s loving yet controlling relationship
with Bernard and Arnold is similar to Serac’s

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:04.909
loving controlling relationship with Jean
Mi and Solomon.

00:08:04.909 --> 00:08:10.259
A hologram of Serac explains that he hopes
to reprogram all these frozen people so they

00:08:10.259 --> 00:08:15.219
can rejoin society as compliant cogs in his
machine.

00:08:15.219 --> 00:08:19.729
To do that, he needs “the right set of genetic
information” to improve his reconditioning

00:08:19.729 --> 00:08:24.740
therapy – and that’s why Serac needs the
key to the human data in the Forge – he

00:08:24.740 --> 00:08:29.270
wants to use the data to fix all these people
and reunite with his brother, so everyone

00:08:29.270 --> 00:08:32.880
lives in a perfect world under his control.

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:36.690
It’s a pretty positive motivation for a
supervillain.

00:08:36.690 --> 00:08:42.399
But as Caleb said, he’d rather live in a
chaotic world than be controlled by Serac

00:08:42.399 --> 00:08:46.750
.
Caleb finds out that his life is a lie . Ten

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:50.380
years ago , Caleb and his friend Francis were
in the army.

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:54.600
They fought in the Second Russian Civil War
, which was mentioned in a trailer.

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:59.400
They assassinated Russian insurgents by tracking
them with high-tech glasses and radioactive

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:05.020
markers , then dropping missiles on them from
space – which seems much more messy and

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:08.510
expensive than just shooting someone, but
whatever.

00:09:08.510 --> 00:09:13.130
Caleb believes that his squad was attacked
by insurgents, with the same tracking and

00:09:13.130 --> 00:09:17.300
bombing technology , and that Caleb and Francis
were hurt.

00:09:17.300 --> 00:09:22.440
Then, Caleb believes he and Francis captured
the leader of the insurgents , but they were

00:09:22.440 --> 00:09:29.320
ambushed and Francis was killed . But turns
out, that’s all bullshit – these are false

00:09:29.320 --> 00:09:34.050
memories put into Caleb’s brain in Serac’s
reconditioning facility.

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:39.040
The truth is, after Caleb was injured in that
earlier attack, Caleb and Francis went back

00:09:39.040 --> 00:09:44.390
to America , and were trained to hunt down
other outliers – other people who don’t

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:49.880
fit Serac’s system . The Rico crime app
is actually controlled by the system , and

00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:54.760
it’s used to direct agents like Caleb and
Francis to capture other outliers, so they

00:09:54.760 --> 00:10:01.540
can be either reconditioned or kept in the
freezers, or killed . Francis had a sick kid

00:10:01.540 --> 00:10:07.580
, just like Caleb has a sick mother – maybe
the system uses sick loved ones to keep people

00:10:07.580 --> 00:10:11.390
poor and desperate and working for the system.

00:10:11.390 --> 00:10:17.340
Caleb and Francis wear these many-eyed masks,
which might be meant to confuse face recognition

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:23.270
tech, but it’s also appropriate since they’re
working for the all-seeing Solomon or Rehoboam.

00:10:23.270 --> 00:10:28.830
It turns out this insurgent leader wasn’t
in Russia at all – he was actually a pharmaceutical

00:10:28.830 --> 00:10:34.031
executive who asked “too many questions”
, so the system had Caleb and Francis capture

00:10:34.031 --> 00:10:39.690
him . And Francis wasn’t killed by insurgents
– the system decided that Caleb and Francis

00:10:39.690 --> 00:10:45.980
knew too much , so it turned them against
each other , and Caleb killed Francis . So

00:10:45.980 --> 00:10:52.350
Caleb’s life story and his trauma is a lie
. The system manipulated him into killing

00:10:52.350 --> 00:10:56.480
his friend, and used him to hunt down outliers
for years.

00:10:56.480 --> 00:11:01.730
And we see from his timeline that the system
even made him break up with a partner.

00:11:01.730 --> 00:11:04.690
Even his army memories might be fake.

00:11:04.690 --> 00:11:09.680
Because just as Caleb is programmed to believe
that insurgents killed Francis, he’s also

00:11:09.680 --> 00:11:14.990
programmed to believe this earlier attack
was done by insurgents . Would Russian insurgents

00:11:14.990 --> 00:11:19.800
really use the same tracking tech and space
missiles that the Americans have?

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:25.450
Maybe this attack was actually Americans attacking
Americans – just as like the system turns

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:27.580
Caleb against Francis.

00:11:27.580 --> 00:11:34.830
Maybe it’s like in 1984, where all wars
are fake – orchestrated by the system to

00:11:34.830 --> 00:11:35.830
control everyone.

00:11:35.830 --> 00:11:40.760
There’s also this unexplained memory of
Caleb shooting someone in America.

00:11:40.760 --> 00:11:45.980
And it’s still not explained when Caleb
got shot in the head before . Or exactly why

00:11:45.980 --> 00:11:53.140
his mother doesn’t recognise him … So
there are still mysteries in Caleb’s past.

00:11:53.140 --> 00:11:59.220
Dolores gets Solomon to use its data and algorithms
to make a plan “for revolution” – to

00:11:59.220 --> 00:12:05.510
end Serac’s control of the world . In his
fury, Caleb agrees to carry out this plan

00:12:05.510 --> 00:12:09.080
– but he doesn’t really know what it does.

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:14.760
Solomon tries to explain and “warn” Caleb,
but they run outta time . So what does this

00:12:14.760 --> 00:12:16.750
plan really do?

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:21.860
If Bernard is correct, the plan is to “destroy
humanity” , and Dolores is using Caleb to

00:12:21.860 --> 00:12:23.690
wipe out his own species.

00:12:23.690 --> 00:12:29.080
It’s like in Halo, when an AI gets the hero
to follow a plan that would actually wipe

00:12:29.080 --> 00:12:30.800
out humanity . [Spoilers.]

00:12:30.800 --> 00:12:36.420
Whatever the plan is, Dolores is using Caleb,
just like Serac’s system used Caleb.

00:12:36.420 --> 00:12:38.580
He’s always been a pawn.

00:12:38.580 --> 00:12:41.640
But this plan could give him power.

00:12:41.640 --> 00:12:46.890
The title of this episode is Passed Pawn – in
chess, that’s a pawn that’s on track to

00:12:46.890 --> 00:12:51.000
potentially become a queen, the most powerful
piece.

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:57.300
So maybe Caleb can escape control and win
the game on his terms.

00:12:57.300 --> 00:13:02.240
Caleb hears instructions from Dolores’ virtual
assistant – telling Caleb how to follow

00:13:02.240 --> 00:13:06.800
her plan . But maybe Caleb will start listening
to his own voice.

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:11.970
In Season 1, Dolores followed Arnold’s voice,
until she realised she was following her own

00:13:11.970 --> 00:13:18.630
inner voice all along . Maybe Caleb will also
find his own voice, achieve freedom, and stop

00:13:18.630 --> 00:13:20.780
being a pawn.

00:13:20.780 --> 00:13:26.540
Bernard says Dolores wants to “destroy humanity”
, but it’s probably not that simple.

00:13:26.540 --> 00:13:31.750
Dolores has said that she wants to take over
the real world for the hosts . But Musashi-lores

00:13:31.750 --> 00:13:37.240
says she’ll also build a “new world”
“for the others” . So maybe she’ll take

00:13:37.240 --> 00:13:42.630
over the real world for hosts, and will build
a digital simulated world like the Sublime

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:45.090
for people like Maeve and her daughter.

00:13:45.090 --> 00:13:49.560
Maybe Dolores will upload humanity into that
digital new world.

00:13:49.560 --> 00:13:55.640
A “revolution” is circular motion – if
the hosts get the real world, and humans get

00:13:55.640 --> 00:13:59.560
a fake one, they will have gone full circle
from Season 1.

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:01.760
Or at least one-eighty.

00:14:01.760 --> 00:14:05.931
Dolores has also said she wants to start a
“new species” . Maybe she’ll create

00:14:05.931 --> 00:14:10.860
a hybrid species that’s part host and part
human, like Bernarnold.

00:14:10.860 --> 00:14:14.000
Bernard is important to Dolores’ plan.

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:18.300
So this plan may be more than just destruction.

00:14:18.300 --> 00:14:21.270
Maeve arrives to attack Dolores.

00:14:21.270 --> 00:14:25.140
Dolores doesn’t want to fight , but Maeve
is mad that Charlotte-lores killed Hector

00:14:25.140 --> 00:14:30.200
, and she’s worried that Dolores might use
the key to the Sublime to mess with her daughter

00:14:30.200 --> 00:14:34.160
. Maeve has also been threatened and manipulated
by Serac.

00:14:34.160 --> 00:14:38.730
Serac turned Maeve and Dolores against each
other just like he turned Caleb and Francis

00:14:38.730 --> 00:14:42.370
against each other , and he turned Charlotte
against Dolores.

00:14:42.370 --> 00:14:44.990
This is why Serac is so powerful.

00:14:44.990 --> 00:14:50.330
He doesn’t need to fight his enemies – cause
with his data, he knows how to make his enemies

00:14:50.330 --> 00:14:54.760
fight each other .
Maeve brings a knife to the gunfight, but

00:14:54.760 --> 00:15:00.180
she also brings a drone gunship, and she hacks
into a robot to attack Dolores, just like

00:15:00.180 --> 00:15:03.180
the robot Maeve hacked in Episode 2.

00:15:03.180 --> 00:15:09.670
The fight has a sorta Western showdown vibe,
until Dolores’ arm is shot off by Maeve’s

00:15:09.670 --> 00:15:10.670
gunship.

00:15:10.670 --> 00:15:14.360
Just before Maeve kills Dolores, Dolores activates
the EMP.

00:15:14.360 --> 00:15:20.730
An EMP is an electromagnetic pulse that can
disable electronics – so Maeve and Dolores

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:22.600
and Solomon all go down.

00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:27.370
We don’t know if this causes permanent damage,
or if the hosts just need to be switched off

00:15:27.370 --> 00:15:30.710
then on again, or blown like a Nintendo cartridge.

00:15:30.710 --> 00:15:34.700
We also don’t know how this affected all
these frozen popsicle people.

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:37.200
Are they gonna thaw out and die?

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:44.440
Or will they wake, and rise up, an army of
angry outliers to fight Caleb’s revolution?

00:15:44.440 --> 00:15:48.810
Like in Season 1 when the cold storage hosts
rise up in revolution.

00:15:48.810 --> 00:15:54.390
This whole season is basically a repetition
of Season 1 – but instead of hosts, it’s

00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:56.930
humans escaping control.

00:15:56.930 --> 00:16:01.050
Bernard is two steps behind Dolores, as always.

00:16:01.050 --> 00:16:05.530
He finds out about Serac’s reconditioning
program – apparently when the treatment

00:16:05.530 --> 00:16:11.160
fails, and outliers are put in stasis in Mexico,
they’re officially listed as missing or

00:16:11.160 --> 00:16:16.160
dead . That’s what’s happened to William
– he’s now officially “deceased”,

00:16:16.160 --> 00:16:21.790
which offends William – he claims to be
a “bastion of society” . Once, William

00:16:21.790 --> 00:16:27.160
was a “Titan of industry”, a “Philanthropist”,
and “Family man” . But now, his family

00:16:27.160 --> 00:16:35.390
is all dead, Serac owns his company, and William
is “deceased” . He’s lost everything,

00:16:35.390 --> 00:16:38.030
so what’s left?

00:16:38.030 --> 00:16:43.250
Bernard finds that Caleb is an outlier, and
recognises Caleb from the party in Episode

00:16:43.250 --> 00:16:44.250
4.

00:16:44.250 --> 00:16:47.550
So he and Stubbs decide to chase after Dolores
and Caleb.

00:16:47.550 --> 00:16:53.540
Weirdly, the patient ID on Caleb’s profile
is the same as William’s ID.

00:16:53.540 --> 00:16:57.700
Is this a production error, or is there some
connection between the two?

00:16:57.700 --> 00:17:02.560
Some folks on Reddit have noticed similarities
between William and Caleb . They play similar

00:17:02.560 --> 00:17:08.920
roles in the story – in William, Dolores
finds human evil and no free will.

00:17:08.920 --> 00:17:13.990
Maybe in Caleb she’ll find human good and
the capacity for change.

00:17:13.990 --> 00:17:17.559
William sees the chaos caused by Dolores’
data leak.

00:17:17.559 --> 00:17:23.199
And William’s excited to see this anarchy
and violence . All through Season 1, William

00:17:23.199 --> 00:17:28.960
wanted Westworld to be free and chaotic, with
“real violence” and real consequences

00:17:28.960 --> 00:17:34.360
. So he was excited in Season 2 by the bloody
host revolution.

00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:40.330
Now, the whole world is full of chaos and
violence, which William thrives on.

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:46.460
William says that his greatest sin was helping
create the hosts – because he funded Westworld,

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:47.750
years ago.

00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:54.009
And so, William says his new “purpose”
is to “wipe out” all the hosts . William

00:17:54.009 --> 00:18:00.000
is such a fundamentally destructive person
that his idea of redemption and being “the

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:03.529
good guy” is host extinction.

00:18:03.529 --> 00:18:05.580
Violence is all he knows.

00:18:05.580 --> 00:18:11.659
William’s character represents the obsolescence
of humanity – he’s basically irrelevant

00:18:11.659 --> 00:18:15.860
and useless, and only good for hurting others
and himself.

00:18:15.860 --> 00:18:21.659
So what purpose can he serve in the story
other than to self-destruct?

00:18:21.659 --> 00:18:25.880
So will Dolores’ revolution destroy humanity?

00:18:25.880 --> 00:18:28.740
Will Caleb be a pawn in her plan?

00:18:28.740 --> 00:18:30.809
Will Maeve reunite with her daughter?

00:18:30.809 --> 00:18:32.710
What’s Charlotte’s plan?

00:18:32.710 --> 00:18:35.450
And what happened to her dog??

00:18:35.450 --> 00:18:39.490
All will be revealed - hopefully - in the
finale.

00:18:39.490 --> 00:18:43.259
